  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 極\ntitle: extreme; pole\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-4, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 12\nradical: 木\nradicalNumber: 75\nonyomi: [キョク, ゴク]\nkunyomi: [きわ.める, きわ.まる, きわ.まり, きわ.み, き.める, -ぎ.め, き.まる]\ndistractors: [吸, 急, 橋]\n---\n\n# 極 — extreme; pole\n\n**Strokes:** 12 · **Key (radical):** 木 (no. 75) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n極 concerns an extreme, limit, or pole. 極限 きょくげん is a limit or extreme limit. The adverb 極 ごく means very or extremely and is usually written in kana. The きわめる family concerns reaching an extreme; the separate きめる family concerns deciding or settling.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Notice 木 beside the tightly enclosed right-hand strokes and imagine a marker at the extreme end of a wooden measuring rod. This is a modern-shape mnemonic, not a historical explanation.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| キョク | on | 極限 きょくげん - limit; extreme limit; [消極的](../words/消極的.md) しょうきょくてき - passive; half-hearted; [南極](../words/南極.md) なんきょく - South Pole; Antarctic; [北極](../words/北極.md) ほっきょく - North Pole; Arctic (small っ) |\n| ゴク | on | [極](../words/極.md) ごく - very; extremely (usually written in kana) |\n| きわ.める | kun | [極める](../words/極める.md) きわめる - reach an extreme; take to the limit |\n| きわ.まる | kun | 極まる きわまる - reach an extreme or limit |\n| きわ.まり | kun | 極まり きわまり - limit; end |\n| きわ.み | kun | 極み きわみ - height; peak; limit |\n| き.める | kun | 極める きめる - decide; settle |\n| -ぎ.め | kun | 月極め つきぎめ - monthly contract; bound -ぎめ |\n| き.まる | kun | 極まる きまる - be decided; be settled |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [極](../words/極.md) ごく - very; extremely\n- [極める](../words/極める.md) きわめる - reach an extreme; take to the limit\n- 極限 きょくげん - limit; extreme limit\n- [消極的](../words/消極的.md) しょうきょくてき - passive; half-hearted\n- [南極](../words/南極.md) なんきょく - South Pole; Antarctic\n- [北極](../words/北極.md) ほっきょく - North Pole; Arctic\n\n## Notes\n\n- The linked 極 article teaches the adverb ごく, usually written ごく. Do not follow that link as though it taught a standalone noun きょく.\n- 極める きわめる is transitive and ichidan; 極まる きわまる is intransitive and godan. 極まり きわまり and 極み きわみ are separately listed nouns, not alternative conjugations to substitute freely.\n- The same written 極める can also be きめる, decide or settle; JMdict lists both 決める and 極める for that entry. Its reading row is deliberately not linked to the article teaching きわめる.\n- Kanjipedia lists キョク, ゴク, きわめる, きわまる and きわみ as Joyo readings, and explicitly marks きめる and きまる outside the table. The broader KANJIDIC2 list above is retained. Reading-table status alone does not establish frequency.\n- Kanjipedia explicitly lists 極まる きまる with an outside-Joyo reading marker. JMdict's inspected deciding/settling family instead lists 決まる, 決る and 極る. The external entry establishes the written ま boundary; it is recognition evidence, not a recommendation to prefer 極まる for everyday きまる.\n- 月極め つきぎめ supplies a real bound -ぎめ example, a monthly contract. JMdict also lists 月極 with つきぎめ; its げっきょく reading is flagged irregular and restricted to 月極, not offered as an equal unqualified alternative.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1173880, 1240180, 1240190, 1240300, 1254180, 1255570, 1460180, 1591420, 1591960, 1591970, 2809700, 1520890.\n\nUsage evidence: [Kanjipedia: 極まる きまる](https://www.kanjipedia.jp/kotoba/0001578400); [Kanjipedia notation guide](https://www.kanjipedia.jp/include/popup_kotoba.html); [Kanjipedia: 極める きわめる](https://www.kanjipedia.jp/kotoba/0001580300); [Kanjipedia: 極 reading status](https://www.kanjipedia.jp/kanji/0001577800).\n",
